@page id="b2-fr" rh="BACK MATTER · THE FINAL RULINGS, IN BRIEF · 1 OF 3" m="FINAL RULINGS 0–15"
# The Final Rulings, in brief
The full text is in the Final Rulings register. These are the rulings as the dossiers use them.
tabrl:
| FR | Ruling |
| 0 | Solomon's father is the man Miriam was reassigned to after Thomas left. Solomon stays sixteen and kept the Osei name. Zion was conceived before Thomas left and born after, with no memory of him. |
| 1 | Commonwife is a registration status, not a description. |
| 2 | Thomas's children are Eden, Leah and Zion. Celeste's reclassification absorbs all four. |
| 3 | Thomas left voluntarily in 2084. The record that he relocated was accurate. |
| 4 | Eden entered Celeste's household in 2085, after Thomas had gone. The others stayed with Miriam until 2090. |
| 5 | Two waves: Eden alone in 2085, the younger three together in 2090. |
| 6 | Miriam left all four with Celeste and went alone. Whether each child forgives her isn't decided. |
| 7 | They were never in her father's household. She found him after they were placed. |
| 8 | She may have meant to come back. Celeste heard the instability under the promise. |
| 9 | She was protecting them from the reassigned household and the search. Whether also from herself stays open. |
| 10 | The reclassification made the household expensive to unmake. |
| 11 | Leah watched her pack. Eden was told to take Zion outside. Solomon was two. |
| 12 | "She's coming back," for about a year, then nothing. |
| 13 | Eden remembers a task. Zion remembers the yard and has never said so. |
| 14 | Leah remembers a decision, so she's the angriest and the one who defends Miriam. |
| 15 | Being unreachable wasn't selective. |

@page rh="BACK MATTER · THE FINAL RULINGS, IN BRIEF · 2 OF 3" m="FINAL RULINGS 16–31"
# The Final Rulings, continued
tabrl:
| FR | Ruling |
| 16 | One letter in 2094, intercepted. Celeste never knew of it and has no proof Miriam survived. Who intercepted it stays open. |
| 17 | Miriam's father was Crownward-resident and close to the Vanes, and surviving an unregistered ceremony wasn't an oversight. |
| 18 | She returns with conviction, expecting not to be believed, because the arrangement that kept her away ended. Her father knows there are children, and learned of Eden when the Trial went public. |
| 19 | The other eleven are married down the elite ladder. Nobody goes home unassigned. |
| 20 | The heir may choose any of the twelve. "Without deviation" is a record, not a rule. |
| 21 | Winning means being the choice that costs the Crown nothing. |
| 22 | Refusal is abstention, and the recommendation stands. |
| 23 | No downgrade once announced, except for a dynastic emergency. A candidate's death doesn't count. |
| 24 | A candidate who dies has her status restored to her family, with no compensation and no punishment. |
| 25 | Rejected candidates are married down, and the rejection follows them in the room. |
| 26 | One Covenant Daughter per Dominion. Hannah's twelve girls are her career. |
| 27 | Eligibility isn't entry. Naomi may self-nominate. |
| 28 | Elite husbands are chosen by committee and ranked by standing. A man may decline the assignment, and two have. |
| 29 | If Eden wins, Hannah enters Naomi. If Eden dies or is rejected, Hannah gets her out. |
| 30 | Naomi doesn't know about 2085. |
| 31 | Naomi's father is on the elite ladder below Crown level, living, outside the household. |

@page rh="BACK MATTER · THE FINAL RULINGS, IN BRIEF · 3 OF 3" m="FINAL RULINGS 32–44"
# The Final Rulings, continued
tabrl:
| FR | Ruling |
| 32 | Children are classified by household registration, not parentage or appearance. |
| 33 | Hannah's daughter keeps the name Naomi. The Prelate is renamed, and "Nomi" is rejected as too close. |
| 34 | The 2085 cohort know each other, went home with no placements, and don't activate before book two. |
| 35 | Dorian's removed parent was Elias's elder child. Crest is Dorian's uncle. |
| 36 | The removal was in 2061, when Dorian was a child. |
| 37 | Crest was aware and didn't act. |
| 38 | Dorian was spared because a child's claim can be supervised. |
| 39 | Succession by survivorship. The 2085 Trial was cancelled for the transition, and 2104 is the 39th. |
| 40 | Crest preserved the documents. |
| 41 | Azrael found them during a Crown advisory access period. |
| 42 | Dorian removed them the week Azrael was declared dead. |
| 43 | A document Azrael had read and returned was one Dorian controlled. |
| 44 | Dorian has known the ledger names Elias since 2061. |
small: The Final Rulings register closes with the Prelate's working name, Aurelia, marked POSSIBLE.

@page id="b2-super" rh="BACK MATTER · SUPERSEDED AND IN CONFLICT · 1 OF 2" m="SUPERSEDED; CONFLICT"
# Where the files disagree about these people
rec:
SUPERSEDED · ages | Solomon at thirteen (TL). Zion at nineteen (MEN). Dorian at sixty-one (CR). Leah as the older sister (TL).
SUPERSEDED · Thomas | "Thomas Osei disappears," and Celeste "always believed otherwise" (TL). He left voluntarily (FR 3).
SUPERSEDED · Celeste | An earlier round had her knowing Miriam was alive. She has no proof (FR 16).
SUPERSEDED · names | Calla Hart (TL), now Merritt. Prelate Naomi (TR, CR) and Prelate Huldah (AM), now renamed (FR 33). Crest as Dorian's father (CR).
CONFLICT · Miriam's birth | Born "in Aurelia" in 2062, and Celeste settles there in 2071 (TL).
CONFLICT · Zion's Speaking | "Two years ago," with Eden away watching the Trials (MEN). At eighteen it was 2103, and she was home.
CONFLICT · Leah's review | "Living under Temple review" (TL), and no formal note filed yet (MEN).
CONFLICT · Calla's mother | A Covenant Daughter in the 32nd Trial (TL), which was 2097, when Calla was fourteen.
CONFLICT · Dorian in 2061 | "A child" (FR 36), and about sixteen by his birth year.
CONFLICT · the ledger | Azrael doesn't put it back, and it vanishes from the east wing archive in 2100 (TL).

@page rh="BACK MATTER · SUPERSEDED AND IN CONFLICT · 2 OF 2" m="CONFLICT"
# Where the files disagree, continued
rec:
CONFLICT · Maren | Eliminated before the Social Policy debate, and knocked unconscious on Endurance Day 3 (TR).
CONFLICT · Vivienne | Eliminated before the Social Policy debate, and extracted on Endurance Day 1 (TR).
CONFLICT · Delphine | Extracted on Day 1, and with Eden on Day 3 (TR).
CONFLICT · the final checkpoint | "One of the four women," and five who finish (TR).
CONFLICT · Sera's decision | On the Settling's first day, and forty minutes into the Forum (TR).
CONFLICT · the Declaration | Eden wins (TR), and it's "the moment that will be taken from her" (CR).
prompt: A conflict I've found since this printing | fill

